    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Reed Words: specialist copywriting and verbal-identity studio, founded 2013 by Mike Reed and Wendy Martin. ~20 people across offices in London, Manchester (UK) and New York (US). B Corp. Brand voice, naming and language strategy for big clients (Formula 1, Calm, Heinz, Penhaligons, Google, Sony, Meta). Hands-on craft studio (writers), so Studio rather than full-service agency despite their own about copy. Established, senior leadership; high autonomy as a studio. Tagged Copywriting + Brand strategy (verbal identity sits across both). Sources: their own site/about, Creative Lives in Progress, LinkedIn, founder interview. Work captured: F1 TOV guidelines spreads, Heinz website copy, Penhaligons product descriptions, THIS plant-based TOV guidelines, KHOY naming (before/after). IG headless blocked (error page); queued to ig-queue.json for logged-in grab.",
